# What can go wrong

## 1. Too much shared memory
Agents drown in context.

Fix:
- namespace memory
- summarize aggressively
- retrieve only relevant context

## 2. Agents overlap too much
They do duplicate work.

Fix:
- narrow roles
- enforce handoff formats
- define ownership clearly

## 3. No locking
Parallel agents overwrite each other.

Fix:
- claim tasks atomically
- allow one active owner
- version task updates

## 4. Endless loops
Agents keep reassigning work forever.

Fix:
- retry caps
- escalation thresholds
- human review checkpoints

## 5. Unsafe self-improvement
System mutates itself into nonsense.

Fix:
- keep improvements to prompts, heuristics, routing
- require approval for structural changes

